facts=[
 ('FAC-SAVE01','Global metadata explicitly exposes safariState and bugContestState. Its ordinary initializer sets each nil after prior Phone/regional-dex/DayCare initialization. A failure earlier can prevent those assignments; no guarantee of constructor success from class identity alone.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE02','The complete global_metadata registration is outer class PokemonGlobalMetadata, save getter returns the same $PokemonGlobal object, load callback assigns the validated object to that global. It is nonboot/nonreset and has supplier PokemonGlobalMetadata.new. There is no per-Safari/Contest inner schema check in this Value constraint.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE03','compile_save_hash asks all registered getters and validates each returned outer type before output-key assignment. save_to_file compiles before opening wb, then passes the whole compiled hash to Marshal.dump; no projection that individually removes safari/contest fields appears in these definitions. This proves the request/object boundary, not a native Marshal successful graph roundtrip.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE04','get_data_from_file returns a first Hash unchanged; otherwise reads sequential objects to EOF and adapts via registered old-format callbacks. All17 default blocks have none, so legacy adaptation can yield{}. No native serialized class/version compatibility is guaranteed just by a Ruby class existing.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE05','Game.load validates outer Hash and loads every not-loaded registration before resetting uptime anchor, incrementing sessions, restoring map/autoplay/updateMap and finally assigning scene. Each Value validates then calls restore then marks loaded; earlier restored globals/flags persist after later failure. Loaded registration is skipped; missing key with supplier takes new-game value, separately from aggregate nil-default validity.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE06','Normal map-scene title branch marks nonboot or reset registrations unloaded before assigning title scene. Thus global_metadata normally becomes eligible for a later new-game supplier; boot/nonreset settings stay loaded. Do not infer every arbitrary direct Game.start_new call unconditionally resets a previously loaded global metadata object.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE07','Conversion selection snapshots saved engine version or18.1 and game version or0.0.0. It visits engine category then game, sorts configured version thresholds by PluginManager.compare_versions ascending and preserves per-threshold registration order, selecting savedVersion<threshold. Native/version comparator details are not executed here.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE08','Full run_conversions returnsfalse without backup when selected set empty. Otherwise first wb/Marshal backups to default SaveData::FILE_PATH.bak (not the custom read path), then logs/runs conversions in order. Value procs require stored keys and run before an optional whole-hash proc. Earlier object/file changes remain if later logging/callback/error fails; version markers are written only after all conversions and final console message normally return.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE09','After full conversion success, engine and game markers are overwritten with current constants and run_conversions returnstrue; read_from_file then directly wb-writes the caller file_path. Backup can already exist before any conversion, and converted object prefix/markers can remain in memory if later caller write fails. None of this is an atomic save/rollback guarantee.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE10','run_single_conversions selects the same list from the supplied saved context, invokes only a matching per-value proc on the supplied object, skips whole-hash procs, does not create full-run backup/log/final markers and does not advance supplied context. Subsequent calls can reselect the same list.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE11','All14 complete fixed default conversion bodies are included and manually indexed below. None explicitly reads/writes safariState or bugContestState or defines a named mode-specific format converter. This supports the finite absence of a dedicated default converter; it does not prove all legacy nested state is compatible, all indirectly aliasedPokemon are untouched, or that arbitrary plugin converters are absent.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE12','Game.save sets safesave, increments count, writes magic/time before compile/write. Only IOError/SystemCallError in its begin decrements save_count; type/supplier/callback failures and other exceptions differ. Earlier memory and file prefixes remain, and wb can truncate. Native disk/scene/whole-game execution stays NOT_EXECUTED.'),
 ('FAC-SAVE13','A successful outer restore of metadata can expose stored mode-state objects to the facility getters unchanged by this assignment; their class fields/ongoing flags/cleanup/map-local and result consumers must be joined by the actual facility reviewer. Missing or incompatible inner field repair is not provided by the outer type predicate or by merely listing14 converters.')]
